  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q35-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "35",
    "prompt": "Suppose $p>3$ is a prime number.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q35-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that $p$ can be written in the form $6k\\pm1$ for some $k\\in\\mathbb{Z}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$p=6k\\pm1$ for some $k\\in\\mathbb{Z}$.\n\nThe other remainder classes modulo $6$ have a factor of $2$ or $3$.",
          "worked": "The division algorithm gives $p=6m+r$, where $m\\in\\mathbb{Z}$ and $r\\in\\{0,1,2,3,4,5\\}$. Since $p>3$ is prime, it is divisible by neither $2$ nor $3$.\n\nRemainders $0,2,4$ give an even number, and remainder $3$ gives a multiple of $3$. Thus only remainders $1$ and $5$ remain.\n\nIf $r=1$, then $p=6m+1$. If $r=5$, then\n$$\\begin{align*}p&=6m+5\\\\p&=6(m+1)-1.\\end{align*}$$\nHence $p=6k\\pm1$ for some $k\\in\\mathbb{Z}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q35-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Prove that $p^2-1$ is divisible by $24$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$24\\mid(p^2-1)$.\n\nUsing $p=6k\\pm1$ gives $p^2-1=12k(3k\\pm1)$, and $k(3k\\pm1)$ is even.",
          "worked": "From part (a), $p=6k+1$ or $p=6k-1$ for some integer $k$.\n\nIf $p=6k+1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}p^2-1&=(6k+1)^2-1\\\\p^2-1&=36k^2+12k\\\\p^2-1&=12k(3k+1).\\end{align*}$$\nIf $p=6k-1$,\n$$\\begin{align*}p^2-1&=(6k-1)^2-1\\\\p^2-1&=36k^2-12k\\\\p^2-1&=12k(3k-1).\\end{align*}$$\nIf $k$ is even, each product contains an additional factor of $2$. If $k$ is odd, both $3k+1$ and $3k-1$ are even. In either case, $p^2-1$ is a multiple of $12\\times2=24$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 92
      }
    ]
  },
